Data and generated evidence

The commercial case uses the pinned SSC 8790-heliostat coordinate table and
the SolarPILOT Daggett TMY2 weather file. Their paths, revisions and provenance
are in cases/commercial-reference/case_manifest.json. The raw layout and
weather files stay in the dependency checkouts. Source terms also continue
to apply to imported parameters in the case manifest, upstream receiver
settings in benchmarks/results/phase3a-reference-inventory.json, and
imported geometry and input settings in the Phase 3A commercial case and
grid reports. CC0 covers the project's own measurements, simulations and
derived statistics. It excludes third-party input material and reproduced
notices or excerpts, wherever they occur. Check the asset terms before
redistributing any raw inputs. A public download alone does not grant
permission to redistribute it.

Conditions to check before binary distribution

- SolarPILOT and SolTrace license clauses 1 and 2 require their notices,
  conditions and disclaimer to travel with source and binary redistributions
  in the form specified by each license. Clause 3 requires a redistributing
  research entity to make the entire corresponding source publicly available
  under that license for as long as the redistribution is available.
- Under clause 4, a modified distribution covered by the SolarPILOT license
  must use a distinct, non-confusing designation and identify the underlying
  Alliance software as SolarPILOT(TM). Other uses of a restricted designation
  for the modified version require prior written consent from Alliance.
  SolTrace has the analogous requirement for its designation. Before packaging,
  review the product name, archive name, Python API branding and library
  filename (including solarpilot.so) against the components actually distributed.
  The SSC native code's BSD-3-Clause notices remain separately applicable.
- Verify the linked components and applicable file-level terms. In particular,
  check LGPL 2.1 section 6 requirements for corresponding library source and a
  compliant way to relink where the LGPL applies to the statically linked
  libraries. Account for any redistributed CUDA runtime and Python packages.

